# Button system

Living preview: `/style-guide`. Spec: `DESIGN.md`.

## Canonical classes (compose these)

| Role | Class | Use |
|------|-------|-----|
| Primary | `.btn-primary` | Default CTA (shop, submit, continue) — `#2563EB` |
| Secondary | `.btn-secondary` (alias `.btn-outline`) | Outline on light UI |
| Muted | `.btn-muted` | Quiet form actions |
| Accent | `.btn-accent` | Brand orange CTAs — `#DF3601` (AA) |
| Accent soft | `.btn-accent-soft` | Soft orange **on dark only** |
| Inverse | `.btn-inverse` | White fill on dark bands |
| Inverse outline | `.btn-inverse-outline` | White border on dark |
| Ghost | `.btn-ghost` / `.btn-ghost-on-dark` | Tertiary text CTAs |
| Destructive | `.btn-destructive` | Unsubscribe / sign-out |

Sizes: `.btn-sm` | `.btn-md` | `.btn-lg`

## Rules

1. **Do not invent new button fill colors** (no sky/indigo/Tailwind `orange-500`/`orange-600` for CTAs).
2. Feature classes may keep layout names (`cta-band-btn-primary`) but **must `@apply` a canonical role** for colors.
3. Never white text on `#FF4E00` — use `--acdw-orange-button` (`#DF3601`) via `.btn-accent`.
4. Prefer one primary per view (blue **or** accent orange, not both competing).
5. **Never `.btn-secondary` on dark/black backgrounds** — blue outline fails AA on black (4.06:1). Use `.btn-inverse-outline` or `.btn-inverse`.
6. Before adding a new button style, check `/style-guide` and `DESIGN.md`.
